msgid "At this point you should have working firmware on the board. If you want to load new firmware you will need to follow steps 2-7 again (you cannot use Mission Planner to load firmware). If you are certain that you will never want to load betaflight on the board then you can install the ArduPilot bootloader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards.rst:178
#: 203209fa14bc47888d24af6d3b49c6d1
msgid "Installing the ArduPilot bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards.rst:180
#: c0620e1bed104ce4b2e06970c409c15b
msgid "installing the ArduPilot bootloader is a one-way operation. You cannot restore the board to factory configuration or load betaflight after this step - you would have to return the board to Seriously Pro to be re-flashed with factory firmware, assuming that is possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards.rst:182
#: b7b005f1ca584aa198a620c81b24fae9
msgid "**If you are certain that you only want to use ArduPilot on the board**, then flashing the ardupilot bootloader enables much simpler subsequent upgrades."
